NetHack has a built in notepad... hit ! to escape to a shell, open a
file with your favorite text editor, make changes or browse for
information.  Close file.  Type exit to return to NetHack.

If you're playing in linux console mode, you should have several
available consoles that you can toggle between using ctrl-shift-F1,
ctrl-shift-F2, etc.  That way, you can keep your notes file open!  As
for grep, vi has all sorts of searching functions.  I'm sure emacs
does too (after all, it has everything including the kitchen sink,
much like NetHack).  Of course, if you're playing in a graphical
environment, you can just open another application in another window.

Failing that, you can name most items.  Haven't you ever had 'blessed
+3 silver dragon scale mail named FOOBIE BLETCH=amnesia' or 'a wand of
lightning (0:2) named portal on DL13'?

